# Options to pass to chronyd (chrony.service).
# -F 1: seccomp filter (Debian default).
# -s: at start, set the clock from the drift file's modification time when
#     that is later than both the clock and the RTC.  The carrier RTC is
#     not backed, so after a power loss this restores the time chronyd
#     last wrote the drift file (about hourly, and at stop).
DAEMON_OPTS="-F 1 -s"
